<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office"
      xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
    <title>Frontend Integration Guide</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; }
        h1 { color: #2E74B5; }
        h2 { color: #2E74B5; margin-top: 20px; }
        h3 { color: #5B9BD5; }
        pre { background-color: #F2F2F2; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #D9D9D9; }
        code { font-family: Consolas, monospace; }
        .note { font-style: italic; color: #555555; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Frontend Integration Guide (MVC Views)</h1>
    <p>This document outlines the necessary changes required in the frontend (MVC Views) to integrate with the newly implemented backend features: Recurrence, Status updates, and File Attachments.</p>

    <hr/>

    <h2>1. Task Status Dropdown</h2>
    <p>The <code>TodoTaskStatus</code> enum now needs to be exposed in the UI for users to update the status of their tasks.</p>

    <h3>Where to add:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Views/Task/Create.cshtml</code></li>
        <li><code>Views/Task/Edit.cshtml</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What to add:</h3>
    <p>Add a dropdown bound to the <code>Status</code> property using the <code>Html.GetEnumSelectList</code> helper.</p>

    <pre><code>
&lt;div class="form-group mb-3"&gt;
    &lt;label asp-for="Status" class="form-label"&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;select asp-for="Status" class="form-select" asp-items="Html.GetEnumSelectList&lt;PersonalToDo_Freelance.Domain.Enums.TodoTaskStatus&gt;()"&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;span asp-validation-for="Status" class="text-danger"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
    </code></pre>

    <hr/>

    <h2>2. Recurrence Days of Week Checkboxes</h2>
    <p>For Weekly recurrences, the backend uses a bitwise flag <code>DaysOfWeekFlags</code> to determine which days the task occurs on.</p>

    <h3>Where to add:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Views/Task/Create.cshtml</code> (inside the recurrence section)</li>
        <li><code>Views/Task/Edit.cshtml</code> (inside the recurrence section)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What to add:</h3>
    <p>When the recurrence type is set to <code>Weekly</code>, you need to show checkboxes for each day of the week.</p>

    <pre><code>
&lt;!-- Only show this block if Recurrence.Type == Weekly --&gt;
&lt;div class="form-group mb-3" id="weekly-days-selection"&gt;
    &lt;label class="form-label"&gt;Days of Week&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;div&gt;
        @@foreach (var day in Enum.GetValues(typeof(PersonalToDo_Freelance.Domain.Enums.DaysOfWeekFlags)).Cast&lt;PersonalToDo_Freelance.Domain.Enums.DaysOfWeekFlags&gt;().Where(d =&gt; d != PersonalToDo_Freelance.Domain.Enums.DaysOfWeekFlags.None))
        {
            &lt;div class="form-check form-check-inline"&gt;
                &lt;input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="Recurrence.SelectedDays" value="@@day" 
                       @@(Model.Recurrence != null && Model.Recurrence.SelectedDays.Contains(day) ? "checked" : "")&gt;
                &lt;label class="form-check-label"&gt;@@day.ToString()&lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        }
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
    </code></pre>
    <p class="note">Note: Make sure your ViewModel binds these checkboxes to the <code>Recurrence.SelectedDays</code> list.</p>

    <hr/>

    <h2>3. File Attachments</h2>
    <p>The backend now supports uploading and deleting file attachments for tasks.</p>

    <h3>Where to add:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Views/Task/Details.cshtml</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What to add:</h3>
    <p>You need a form to upload new files, and a list of existing files with delete buttons.</p>

    <h4>1. File Upload Form:</h4>
    <p>Make sure the form tag has <code>enctype="multipart/form-data"</code>.</p>

    <pre><code>
&lt;form asp-action="UploadAttachment" asp-controller="Task" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data"&gt;
    &lt;input type="hidden" name="taskId" value="@@Model.Id" /&gt;
    &lt;div class="input-group mb-3"&gt;
        &lt;input type="file" name="file" class="form-control" required /&gt;
        &lt;button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit"&gt;Upload&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
    </code></pre>

    <h4>2. List of Attachments:</h4>
    <p>Display the attachments using the <code>Attachments</code> property in <code>TaskDetailsViewModel</code>.</p>

    <pre><code>
@@if (Model.Attachments != null && Model.Attachments.Any())
{
    &lt;ul class="list-group mt-3"&gt;
        @@foreach (var attachment in Model.Attachments)
        {
            &lt;li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center"&gt;
                &lt;a href="@@attachment.FilePath" target="_blank"&gt;@@attachment.FileName&lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;form asp-action="DeleteAttachment" asp-controller="Task" method="post" class="d-inline"&gt;
                    &lt;input type="hidden" name="attachmentId" value="@@attachment.Id" /&gt;
                    &lt;input type="hidden" name="taskId" value="@@Model.Id" /&gt;
                    &lt;button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger btn-sm" onclick="return confirm('Are you sure?');"&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;/form&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        }
    &lt;/ul&gt;
}
    </code></pre>

    <hr/>

    <h2>Summary for Frontend Dev:</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Bind the <strong>Status</strong> to the Create/Edit forms.</li>
        <li>Bind the <strong>Days of Week Checkboxes</strong> to the <code>Recurrence.SelectedDays</code> property in the ViewModel.</li>
        <li>Add the <strong>File Upload form</strong> and <strong>Attachment list</strong> to the Details view.</li>
    </ol>

</body>
</html>
